{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"The Wind-deer: a past life story","html":"<article id='ja14'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Jātaka </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Stories of Past Lives 14 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Ekakanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Ones </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Sīlavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Ethics </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>4. Vātamigajātaka </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Wind-deer: a past life story </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Na kiratthi rasehi pāpiyo, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Nothing, it seems, is worse than tastes </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Āvāsehi va santhavehi vā; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>in monasteries or meeting places. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Vātamigaṁ gahananissitaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The domesticated Wind-deer </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Vasamānesi rasehi sañjayo”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>was brought under Victor’s sway by tastes. </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>Vātamigajātakaṁ catutthaṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
